{
 "id": "def-coef-semilinear-geometry-ops",
 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Canonical geometric mate and projection words",
 "status": "split",
 "statement": "For the normalized geometric interface of a strict ring tower [def-coef-semilinear-geometry-derived] over its ordinary derived calculus [def-coef-semilinear-derived-calculus] [def-coef-semilinear-system-models], define the coefficient projection map b as the ordinary adjunction mate of the specified coefficient-pullback comparison. Define the push-transition condition as t(GN) followed by evaluation equal to coefficient extension of push evaluation, then b, then the level direct image of t(N); define the pull-transition condition by the inverse coefficient-pullback comparison and the actual source reduction. Define tensor projection as the derived transpose of tensor pullback followed by counit tensor identity, and define level tensor projection by the identical word with the level adjunction. Define projection evaluation as equality between evaluated system tensor projection and that level tensor projection, transported by the specified tensor and pull/push evaluation comparisons.",
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-coef-semilinear-derived-calculus",
  "def-coef-semilinear-system-models",
  "def-coef-semilinear-geometry-derived"
 ],
